source/reference_guide/intro.rst:20: (pydantic) ["pedantic", "anticipant"]  dictionary at run time against a pydantic schema for each key. Values that should be integers and floats are coerced to the correct type where possible; values that should be strings, booleans, lists or dictionaries raise an error if given the wrong type. Which keys are valid depends on the equation set and solver type chosen. A script is provided to check the validity of a control file before submitting a job — see 
